      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45937214",
      "title": "Hacker News comment by prabhatsharma, an OpenObserve maintainer, on 'I can't recommend Grafana anymore'",
      "venue": "Hacker News. Comment text read via the HN Algolia API. Recorded as the marker for a thread-level finding.",
      "speaker": "vendor",
      "published": "2025-11-15",
      "pulled": "2026-09-17",
      "verbatim": "Check OpenObserve https://github.com/openobserve/openobserve. It precisely was built to solve the challenges around grafana nd elastic. This is not a stack that you will need to weave together, just a single binary/container that would suffice for most users' needs - logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, alerts.\n\nDisclosure: I am a maintainer of OpenObserve",
      "unused": "Kept but cited nowhere, as the marker for a finding a re-run needs: the 124-comment Hacker News thread under src:11 is dominated by competing vendors - the VictoriaMetrics founder and a core developer, and this OpenObserve maintainer - arguing their own products. Those comments read like practitioner complaints about Grafana and are not. Nothing in this map draws buyer voice from that thread; only the blog post itself (src:11) is used."
